WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.175
So who does what?

2
00:00:01.175 --> 00:00:03.938
Developers on our own
staff write the code.

3
00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:07.413
A different, qualified
reviewer approves each change.

4
00:00:07.413 --> 00:00:10.774
The change advisory board
approves the move to production.

5
00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:13.528
The security officer
sets the coding rules,

6
00:00:13.528 --> 00:00:17.887
and the agency's Chief AI Officer
decides which AI tools are approved.

7
00:00:17.887 --> 00:00:22.249
The point is that no one person
writes, approves, and deploys.

8
00:00:22.249 --> 00:00:25.288
And we train the people we
already have rather than hiring.

9
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:29.902
They start in a free developer sandbox,
learn our rules before they touch real work,

10
00:00:29.902 --> 00:00:34.313
and pair up with experienced platform
developers for their first few changes.

11
00:00:34.313 --> 00:00:37.787
After that, they can qualify
as reviewers themselves.

12
00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:41.423
Every piece should have at least
two people who can maintain it,

13
00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:44.210
so the application never
depends on one person.
